Exact task statement
Measure how dependent the business is on a small number of customers overall and by Entity.
Build order
21.	Choose an analysis window, ideally trailing 12 months.
22.	Aggregate revenue by customer and rank customers by revenue descending.
23.	Compute cumulative revenue and cumulative share.
24.	Separately calculate top 5, top 10, top 20, and top 50 shares by Entity.
Validation checks
•	Final cumulative share should reach 100 percent.
•	Top 5 share must be less than or equal to top 10 share, and so on.
•	Customer totals must tie to company totals.
Final output template
customer_rank	customer_code	oracle_customer_name	customer_revenue	cumulative_revenue	cumulative_share_pct
1	100234	Customer A	28400000	28400000	4.6%
Output column definitions
•	cumulative_revenue = running sum of customer_revenue by rank.
•	cumulative_share_pct = cumulative_revenue / total company revenue.
•	top_10_share_pct = revenue from top 10 customers divided by total revenue for the same scope.

--====================================================================================================================
With cte_1 as
(Select 
	t.bu,
	t.customer_code,
	t.oracle_customer_name,
	t.industry,
	t.top150_mapping,
	t.amount,
	t.rev_mth_dt,
	p.is_trailing_12m	
From platinum.txn_normalized t
Left Join platinum.period_reference p
on t.rev_mth_dt = p.month_start
Order by t.rev_mth_dt Desc
),
cte_2 as
(Select
	distinct customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	sum(amount) over(partition by customer_code) as customer_ttm_revenue,
	sum(amount) over() as ttm_revenue
From cte_1
Where is_trailing_12m = 1
Group by 
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	amount
Order by
	sum(amount) over(partition by customer_code) Desc
)
Select
	Row_Number() over(order by customer_ttm_revenue desc) as customer_rank,
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	customer_ttm_revenue,
	ttm_revenue,
	Round(coalesce(customer_ttm_revenue / ttm_revenue , 0)*100,2) as cumm_share_pct
From cte_2
	
